# Recipe Cards
// Your recipes:  pick one, set how many are eating, and every amount scales;
// show it in metric or in cups and spoons;  tick ingredients and add them to the shopping list.
// The recipes are in a JSON file, RecipeCards.api.spell says where;  the shopping list is Shopping List's own, imported.

recipe cards is an app
	its "chosen" is a recipe
		// The recipe on show
	its "editing" is a recipe
		// The recipe on its Edit screen, while one is
	its "diners" is a number starting at 4
		// How many are eating
	its "units" is one of metric or cups
		// Grams and millilitres, or cups and spoons
	its "scale" is
		// How much more, or less, than the recipe says
		if its chosen does not exist or the serves of its chosen is 0 return 1
		return its diners / the serves of its chosen
	"aisle list" is a new aisle list
		// Shopping List's own list, by aisle:  the same list, from its CSV file

	when creating it
		// The first time, with an empty file, three recipes to start with
		if there are no recipes
			add the tomato soup
			add the red lentil dal
			add the pancakes
		if that fails
			// The file can't be read just now:  the recipes list says so
			return
		set its chosen to the first of (every recipe)

	group "Units"
	to "show metric" with title "Grams and ml"
		selected when its units is metric
		set its units to metric

	to "show cups and spoons" with title "Cups and spoons"
		selected when its units is cups
		set its units to cups

	to draw it
		<container>
			<stack>
				<toolbar>
					<text size="large" heavy slot="title">Recipe Cards</text>
					<action "show metric" />
					<action "show cups and spoons" />
					<spacer />
					<action "undo" icon-only />
					<action "redo" icon-only />
				</toolbar>
				<grid stackable>
					<column width="5">
						<stack>
							<buttons direction="vertical" fluid basic>
								<for recipe in every recipe>
									<button active={recipe is its chosen} onClick={pick recipe}>{recipe's title}</button>
								</for>
							</buttons>
							<form value={it}>
								<field label="Cooking for">
									<input name="diners" type="number" min="1" labeled="right" label="people" />
								</field>
							</form>
							<header size="small">Shopping list</header>
							<text color="grey" size="small">Ticked ingredients go here, on the Shopping List app's own list</text>
							{draw the aisle list}
						</stack>
					</column>
					<column width="11">
						{draw the screen of it}
					</column>
				</grid>
			</stack>
		</container>

	to draw its screen
		// The Edit screen while a recipe is being changed;  else the chosen recipe's card
		if its editing
			draw (a new recipe editor with recipe = its editing)
		otherwise if its chosen
			draw its chosen
		otherwise
			<text color="grey">Choose a recipe on the left to see its ingredients and steps.</text>
